 "genre_note": "144 notes across 19 sub-plans; 39,217 / 41,402 words assigned (94.7%). No (doc, block) pair is assigned twice \u2014 verified programmatically. No note exceeds 1,800 source words.\n\nBUILDING-BLOCK DISTRIBUTION. Overwhelmingly empirical_observation (~110 notes) and concept (~14), exactly as the brief predicted for news. argument (~14) and counter_argument (~9) appear only where the source genuinely carries a claim-with-grounds or an explicit rebuttal \u2014 mostly in The Roar's opinion pieces (Boycott/Hussain/Atherton on England; Foster denying favouritism; QRU refusing commercial centralisation; Eddie Jones denying Japan contact and defending youth selection) and in a handful of Sporting News analysis passages (USC's turnover margin, the 49ers' cap flexibility, USMNT back-line errors). procedure (2) occurs only in the two sportsbook how-to documents. model occurs exactly ONCE \u2014 `julian_nagelsmann_tactical_system_and_press.md`, the only passage in the cluster that explains a mechanism rather than reporting an event. hypothesis: ABSENT. Nothing in 20 sports documents states a testable prediction with the structure of a hypothesis; the closest candidates (MVP odds, contract projections) are forecasts-as-reported-fact, correctly typed empirical_observation. Manufacturing hypothesis notes here would have been fabrication. navigation: none produced, per instructions.\n\nSHARED ENTITY NOTES (single note, blocks from several documents) \u2014 8 of them, the main multi-hop surface:\n- max_scherzer_back_injury_and_roster_removal (0495 + 0408): pulled in Game 3, off the roster before Game 4.\n- adolis_garcia_oblique_injury (0495 + 0408): injured in Game 3, season over before Game 4.\n- corey_seager_home_runs / marcus_semien_five_rbi (0495 + 0408): each player's decisive contributions across both games.\n- world_series_2023_broadcast_coverage and mlb_2023_postseason_results_bracket (0495 + 0408): these blocks are byte-identical boilerplate in both documents; splitting them would have created two near-duplicate notes and halved the evidence.\n- all_blacks_generational_change and ian_foster_all_blacks_tenure_and_robertson_succession (0022 + 0176): the retirements/Last Dance and the Foster\u2192Robertson handover are told across the final report and the preview.\n- eddie_jones_case_for_reforming_australian_rugby_system (0407 + 0492): Jones's centralisation argument is quoted in both.\n- opening_and_funding_an_online_sportsbook_account (0497 + 0589): the same signup procedure printed in both betting guides.\n- aron_baynes_suspension (0406 + 0240) and (within one doc) zylan_cheatham_leg_injury pulled out of two Round 5 game reports.\n\nSIZE VS COHERENCE. The eight live-blogs (0378, 0408, 0495, 0483, 0534, 0568) were split at game-phase boundaries \u2014 quarter, period, inning group, half \u2014 never at a word count; each split lands on a natural narrative seam. The two NBL roundups (0240, 0406) are the clearest case of the trap the brief warns about: 3,431 and 2,639 words that are actually 8 and 7 unrelated games. They are decomposed one note per game, never merged.\n\nWHAT I DROPPED, AND ONE RECONSIDERATION. Drops are article titles, section headers, \"MORE:\"/\"READ:\" promo links, \"Facebook Twitter Whatsapp\" share bars, \"Advertisement\", \"\u00a9 AAP\", \"Sports opinion delivered daily\", tracking boilerplate (\"The Sporting News tracked updates...\"), and social-media embed captions. On first pass I dropped all tweet blocks; re-inspecting them recovered ~470 words that were NOT contentless reaction \u2014 Bedard's first NHL point (\"first NHL assist for Connor Bedard\"), the Garcia injury confirmation, Scherzer's \"back tightness\", Walker being thrown out by Garcia, and running scorelines. Those are now assigned. Likewise the World Series inning headers (\"Ninth inning: Rangers 3, Diamondbacks 1\") are section headers that also carry the running score, so they were assigned to their inning notes rather than dropped.\n\nDOCUMENTS BELOW 90%, REPORTED HONESTLY. doc_0409 (Cricket World Cup history) is 88.4%: it is written as a Q&A explainer whose section headers are full interrogative sentences (\"When was the first ODI Cricket Word Cup?\", \"Who has won the most ODI Cricket World Cups?\"), which are pure navigation chrome \u2014 the answer text underneath is fully assigned. Every other document is \u226590%; the next lowest are doc_0534 (90.2%, heavy Spanish-language tweet embeds duplicating the English commentary) and doc_0568 (92.2%)."
